# Build-context allowlist for deploy/Dockerfile.
#
# Deny everything, then re-admit exactly what the build copies. An allowlist,
# not a denylist, for the same reason the hatch sdist target uses one: a new
# directory dropped at the repo root (a corpus dump, a scratch DB, the private
# ADR tree) must not silently join the build context.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!constraints.txt
!README.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!CHANGELOG.md
!alembic.ini
!alembic/**
!particles/**
!artifacts/**
!clients/web-ui/dist/**
!design/tokens.css
# The benchmark fixtures the wheel force-includes (particles benchmark
# trip-vs-move / update-gate), listed per file like the force-include.
!tests/fixtures/trip_vs_move/session-04.md
!tests/fixtures/trip_vs_move/session-11.md
!tests/fixtures/trip_vs_move/session-12-moved.md
!tests/fixtures/trip_vs_move/reader-01.md
!tests/fixtures/trip_vs_move/reader-02-moved.md
!tests/fixtures/update_probe/gate_pairs.json
!tests/fixtures/update_probe/gate_pairs_heldout.json
!tests/fixtures/update_probe/past_value_pairs.json
!tests/fixtures/update_probe/past_marker_heldout.json
!deploy/config.container.yaml

# Re-exclude noise that lives inside the admitted trees.
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/**
**/.mypy_cache/**
**/.ruff_cache/**
